{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "A5ZCF7",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Cockpit",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "TN75y",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Cockpit — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "EnWLt",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The daily-driver dashboard — the decision cockpit: one screen, ~20 min, mobile.\n\nEntry: login → /dashboard (main authenticated home).\nScreens: Panorama (Default · Tranquilo · Black swan) → Asset detail (Análisis · Mi posición) → Consolidado (the portfolio lens: patrimonio, equity curve, '¿Valió la pena?', allocation). Desktop (1280, kit 0.5.0): three artboards. Panorama and Consolidado fit without scroll; the asset detail drops from 3048pt to 1400pt.\n\nConsolidado entry points: the Panorama patrimonio hero and Cartera's summary card in assets.pen — one screen, two doors. Its two comparison cards are designed in full but their engine is build-gated and needs TWR, not the money-weighted period returns (D12).\n\nBlocks: PatrimonioStrip (MXN total + Δ día, the door to Consolidado — it was promised by this brief but missing from the artboards until 2026-08-24) + sentiment carousel · 'atención hoy' band · holdings list with semáforo + freshness · (detail) price chart (D2) + confluence semáforo (D3) + señales (RSI/MA/Bollinger) + observations + fundamentals.\n\nGrounding: real data — portfolio value, P&L (MXN, FX at trade), trend-score, RSI/SMA/Bollinger, technical_observations, fundamentals. Confluence engine (Light 2 + window) is design-only, build-gated (D3).\n\nMoney follows D10: the Radar subtitle declares MXN once and rows drop the symbol; anything in another currency carries its ISO prefix (USD 137.00) — including the position grid, which genuinely mixes MXN and USD.\n\nThe Activos tab lives in flows/assets.pen: this file's rows link into it, and the three-tier ladder (Poseo / Sigo / Rastreado) is defined there (D9).\n\nDesktop findings (2026-08-24, panel C5/C1/C4): (a) the sentiment carousel dies on desktop — three columns at the components' native ~309 width show all three cards at once, so nothing is stretched and nothing is cut; (b) the asset detail has NO master list — the Radar is the Panorama's editorialised selection ('con actividad hoy'), not an asset navigator, and reading it beside a 1400pt detail is what made it feel out of place. The master-detail D4 asks for belongs in flows/assets.pen, where the list IS the screen; (c) the reading chain veredicto → chart → semáforo stays in one column, with Señales adjacent — they are the same reading at two resolutions.\n\nKnown canvas limit, not a product constraint: the Chart's plot and its RSI plot are fixed-width drawings (318), so their column is pinned to 350. In code lightweight-charts is responsive (D2, the controller carries a ResizeObserver) — do not copy the pinned width into the ERB.\n\nCopy: es-MX. kit-version-source 0.5.0.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
